<div class="prose max-w-prose">

N&B Calder had already engaged another company to help with a brand and website
refresh, but the project stalled and left them with incomplete assets and a
website that did not reflect the breadth of what they actually offered. They
were still paying for a website that barely scratched the surface of their
business and failed to communicate their expertise.

## The problem

The previous work had not delivered a clear or complete digital presence.
Instead of showcasing the company properly, the site felt unfinished and
underrepresented their services. The challenge was to turn that stalled project
into something that genuinely represented the business and helped convert
visitors into enquiries.

## The rebuild

I created a new website in Webflow that retained the features they valued while
prioritising clarity, conversion, and credibility. The updated site was built to
present their workmanship more effectively, make the offering easier to
understand, and give the business a digital presence that matched the quality
of the work they do.

Rather than a few scattered photos and a contact form, the site became a full
showcase of their capabilities, services, and experience. The structure was
redesigned to guide visitors through the business clearly and help them quickly
understand why N&B Calder is the right choice.

## Why it worked

The project was about restoring trust in the brand and giving the business a
website that actually supports growth. By focusing on what mattered most to the
client and the audience, the new site moved from a partial online presence into
a confident, conversion-focused marketing tool.

You can explore the live site here: [N&B Calder](https://www.nandbcalder.co.uk)

